{"c":[{"name":"20261008T004510Z-16ddc03f0a00f357","text":"Xcode's first privacy phase checks source plists; its last requires the processed bundle plist as an input. Release helper env-file extraction preserves TypeSafe key/provider/model/cap and refuses other providers before spawn.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T030901Z-9525a678a3afd6cf","text":"Disclosure.walk refuses any request-body key outside KEY (no spaces), so ids like 'note 1' cannot be state keys (INT1 uses note_1); a state map with dynamic keys also needs a childGlob rule in privacy/shapes.ts besides its .* row.","type":"note"}]}
